arketing is a strategy used  to encourage  existing sales representatives to  recruit new distributors  who are paid a percentage of their  recruit sales  or just get other salespeople in general  however mlms like arbonne have been  under fire in the media  for its alleged pyramid scheme like  tactic arbonne uses what they call  independent consultants to sell products  you know the people who message you on  facebook that call you babe  and tell you that they've got a business  opportunity for you  yeah those poor souls are harassing you  for money  because they had to pay a 59  registration fee  to become a consultant yes they had to  pay arbonne  to get the job honestly the internet is  filled with so many war stories of  people  minding their own business on instagram  only to get spammed with some  pitch to become a boss babe you  probably have your own anyway according  to a few online blogs and articles  none of which i can substantiate so  please do take this with a grain of salt  but apparently every consultant must  spend 150  each month on arbonne products every  month  in order to earn their commission and if  you don't spend the necessary amount of  money on arbonne products each month  you won't receive commission on your  sales  and will therefore be working for free  please correct that  in the comments if i am wrong but that  is what i was reading online  so who would do that i guess they're  consultants  by signing other people up they reduce  their own  costs now mlms also manage to carefully  word their terms and conditions  in a way that avoids any incriminating  legal issues  if you don't want to become a consultant  you can opt to become  a preferred client where if you pay a 35  registration fee you can get 40 off all  product  however this is just one example of the  type of kind of  sign up and receive discount arbonne  offers to its users  from what i can understand and i'm not a  lawyer kaboom you've been lawyered  all of these tactics a